<article class="legal-document"><div class="legal-heading"><p class="eyebrow">LEGAL NOTICE</p><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p class="lead">How StudyHub handles information when you use the service.</p><p class="legal-meta">Effective date: September 20, 2026</p></div>
<div class="legal-callout"><i data-lucide="info"></i><p>This policy describes the current StudyHub implementation. StudyHub does not currently use Google Analytics and does not currently collect email addresses. If either is introduced, this policy will be updated before or when that change takes effect.</p></div>
<section><h2>1. Who this policy covers</h2><p>This Privacy Policy applies to StudyHub, a not-for-profit student workspace project, and to people who visit or use its website and application. StudyHub is not currently identifying a separate legal entity, mailing address, or privacy contact in this application. Obtain local legal review before launch or public operation.</p></section>
<section><h2>2. Information you provide</h2><p>When you create an account, StudyHub stores your name, username, age, and a password hash. It does not store your plain-text password. You may also provide course names and codes, tasks, due dates, group names and descriptions, comments, resources and URLs, reports, votes, notifications, moderation messages, and other content you submit.</p></section>
<section><h2>3. Information created by use</h2><p>StudyHub creates session records in server memory when you sign in. It uses a strict, HttpOnly, SameSite session cookie to recognize your signed-in browser. Login failures are tracked temporarily by request IP to limit repeated attempts. The server also creates timestamps, membership roles, report records, moderation records, and activity needed to operate shared groups.</p></section>
<section><h2>4. How we use information</h2><ul><li>To create and authenticate accounts.</li><li>To save personal todos, courses, groups, comments, resources, and notifications.</li><li>To show shared content to authorized members and deliver live updates to authorized rooms.</li><li>To prevent abuse, investigate reports, enforce group rules, and operate content moderation.</li><li>To maintain, secure, debug, and improve the service.</li></ul></section>
<section><h2>5. Moderation and outside processors</h2><p>StudyHub uses local scanners and moderation lists. When configured by the operator, content may also be sent to OpenRouter and the configured content-safety model for structured review. Removed text may be placed in a local moderation queue for later review. Submitted URLs may be compared with a known unsafe-URL corpus; the application does not currently use advertising trackers.</p><p>Review the applicable third-party provider policies before enabling those integrations. StudyHub should not be used for highly sensitive personal information.</p></section>
<section><h2>6. Storage and security</h2><p>Current deployments store data in a local SQLite database. The data directory and database are assigned restrictive file permissions. Personal todo data is encrypted with AES-256-GCM at rest. Passwords are hashed with scrypt. These measures reduce risk but cannot guarantee security. Operators must use HTTPS, protect the data volume and encryption key, limit server access, and maintain backups responsibly.</p></section>
<section><h2>7. Sharing</h2><p>StudyHub shares content with the members and moderators who are allowed to access the relevant organization or group. We do not sell personal information or place ads in the current implementation. Information may also be disclosed to service providers used for enabled moderation or when required by law, to protect users, or to investigate misuse.</p></section>
<section><h2>8. Retention, deletion, and your choices</h2><p>The current application does not yet provide a self-service export, deletion, or email-based recovery flow. Data may remain in the local database, backups, moderation records, or account history until an authorized operator removes it. Ask the operator through the available in-app support or moderation channel for access, correction, or deletion requests. Requests may be limited by law, safety needs, or records needed to enforce these rules.</p></section>
<section><h2>9. Children and age limits</h2><p>Accounts are currently limited to people aged 13 or older. This age check alone does not establish compliance with COPPA, GDPR-K, or other child-privacy laws. StudyHub should not knowingly collect information from children where the law requires parental consent or a different service design.</p></section>
<section><h2>10. Future analytics and email</h2><p>Google Analytics is planned as a possible future feature, but is not active today. Email collection and email notifications are also planned possibilities, but are not active today. Before enabling either, StudyHub will document what is collected, why it is collected, how long it is kept, which providers receive it, and any choices or consent required by law.</p></section>
<section><h2>11. Changes</h2><p>StudyHub may update this policy as the service changes. The effective date above will change with material updates. Continued use after an update means the updated policy applies to future use, subject to applicable law.</p></section>
<section><h2>12. Severability</h2><p>If any part of this policy is found invalid or unenforceable, that part will be limited or removed to the minimum extent necessary, and the remaining parts will continue to apply.</p></section>
</article>